    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d487">

                <pb facs="0450" n="334" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg334"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 838.00/737.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Minister Smith to the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Extract.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Port au Prince</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-01-03">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">January 3, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>President Oreste to-day at an interview at his request informed me of the capture
                    yesterday at Thomazeau of one Celestin, Haitian exile and the promoter of the
                    disturbance on the frontier.* * * Oreste attributes Thomazeau troubles to the
                    Dominican military authorities, and requested that the Department be informed as
                    to his belief.* * * Threats have been made against the property of foreigners,
                    according to the best obtainable information.* * * Situation throughout the
                    Republic regarded as exceedingly grave. I would respectfully suggest and urge
                    that a naval vessel be sent here at the earliest possible moment.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Smith</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
